- [Coaching rule: pseudocode-first, real code only on request](feedback_coaching_pseudocode_first.md) — Hard rule for this project: scaffolding/pseudocode by default, full real code only when asked to refine/finish or as a review example.
- [User profile: learning Rust from scratch](user_role.md) — Builds-real-apps learner; wants principles + syntax explained as we co-design.
- [Project: nimbus — distributed KV/stream/queue Rust app](project_nimbus.md) — Co-designed real app named nimbus (Goku's cloud); learning Rust is the primary outcome.
- [Workflow: project-driven, incremental, review-together](feedback_workflow_review_loop.md) — Design together → user codes → review together; I provide scaffolding + examples on request.
- [Always explain acronyms on first use](feedback_explain_acronyms.md) — Expand and briefly explain every technical acronym (WAL, REPL, CQRS, etc.) first time in a session.
- [Use AskUserQuestion (multi-choice) for option lists](feedback_use_multichoice_for_options.md) — Prefer the AskUserQuestion tool over raw-text bullet lists when asking user to pick between options.
- [Tooling intent: rust-analyzer, cargo-watch, CI/CD](project_tooling_intent.md) — Plan for git init + standard Rust dev tooling and CI; specifics TBD as we go.
- [Rust toolchain path + Bash-tool PATH workaround](reference_rust_toolchain_path.md) — Toolchain at ~/.cargo/bin; the Bash tool doesn't source .cargo/env, prepend it or use full paths.
